        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0437" n="321" xml:id="pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 093.11141/23.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Governor of Virginia.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    concerning the desire of the State of Virginia to present to the British
                    Government a replica of Houdon’s statue of Washington, with special reference to
                    your letter of March 26, 1914, I have the honor to enclose a copy of a despatch
                    on the subject from the American Ambassador at London, covering a copy of a note
                    from the Foreign Office making formal acceptance of this gift.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
